  <sector code="12382" percentage="50" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Approximately 50% of the Global Health Research Centre&apos;s activities and resources will be devoted to conducting high quality research into the treatment and management of those living with multiple long-term conditions in India and Nepal, with a specific focus on chronic and non-communicable diseases.</narrative>
  </sector>
  <sector code="11120" percentage="50" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Approximately 50% of the Global Health Research Centre&apos;s activities and resources will be devoted to training and capacity building activities for staff and students affiliated with the LMIC institutions based in India and Nepal. This will include a broad variety of short- and long-form training courses, including MSc/MRes and PhD studentships and short courses for a wide variety of University staff. The primary aim of these activities will be build capacity for these individuals and institutions to support or deliver high quality healthcare research in the future</narrative>
  </sector>
